       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control. Nothing in the details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going above the maximum.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If this is intentional, for example refractory hypertension under specialist guidance, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's an intentional above-maximum dose.\n3. **A different dose or drug**, if 20 mg was a typo or you'd rather add a second agent such as an ARB, ACE inhibitor or thiazide.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
